{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "scheme-maps",
 "title": "IMGT -> Kabat / Chothia position tables for the V-DOMAIN",
 "source": "IMGT Scientific chart, 'Correspondence between the IMGT unique Lefranc numbering and the different numberings (horizontal display)', https://www.imgt.org/IMGTScientificChart/Numbering/IMGTnumberingsTable.html, transcribed cell by cell on 2026-08-13.",
 "licence": "CC BY 4.0 (IMGT data), see imgt-reference.json for the verbatim terms.",
 "citations": {
  "imgt": "Lefranc M-P, The Immunologist 7:132-136 (1999); Lefranc M-P et al., Dev Comp Immunol 27:55-77 (2003), PMID 12477501.",
  "kabat": "Kabat EA et al., Sequences of Proteins of Immunological Interest, NIH Publication 91-3242 (1991).",
  "chothia": "Chothia C and Lesk AM, J Mol Biol 196:901-917 (1987)."
 },
 "notes": [
  "Landmarks that make this transcription checkable: IMGT 23 -> Kabat H22 / L23 (1st-CYS), IMGT 41 -> Kabat H36 / L35 (CONSERVED-TRP), IMGT 104 -> Kabat H92 / L88 (2nd-CYS).",
  "The IMGT chart stops at IMGT 115 and tabulates '-' across the heavy CDR3, because Kabat numbers a CDR3 by its OBSERVED length rather than by a fixed position. CDR3 and FR4 are therefore produced by the length rule in `cdr3Rule` (Kabat 1991: heavy H3 95-102 with insertions at 100, light L3 89-97 with insertions at 95, FR4 continuing at H103 / L98), which reproduces the light-chain cells the chart DOES tabulate (IMGT 112 -> L95A ... IMGT 115 -> L95D) exactly.",
  "Chothia overrides are applied for IMGT 1-104 only; the CDR3 and FR4 of a Chothia view are produced by the Kabat rule and every converted domain says so in its warnings.",
  "Abhinandan & Martin (2008) and AHo (Honegger & Pluckthun 2001) are NOT in this chart and no other obtainable source was transcribed, so they are listed in `unavailable` and convertScheme REFUSES them. A guessed conversion table would renumber residues plausibly and wrongly."
 ],
